ITEMS = ((('how do i use a defibrillator', 'what is a defibrillator for in first aid', 'how does a defibrillator work', 'when should i get a defibrillator', 'what are the steps for using a defibrillator', 'how to operate a defibrillator in an emergency', 'what does a defibrillator do to the heart', 'how do bystanders use a defibrillator', 'what is the purpose of a public defibrillator', 'how to turn on a defibrillator'), 'A defibrillator gives a controlled shock that can help a heart in cardiac arrest return to a normal rhythm. In an emergency, call emergency services, fetch the nearest device and follow its spoken instructions. Do not touch the person while it analyses or delivers a shock.'), (('where can i find a defibrillator near me', 'how do i locate a public defibrillator', 'are defibrillators kept in shops', 'what places have a defibrillator', 'how to ask someone to fetch a defibrillator', 'can i use a defibrillator at school', 'where are defibrillators kept at work', 'how to find a defibrillator in a town centre', 'should i know where the nearest defibrillator is', 'how to check a defibrillator location in advance'), 'Public defibrillators are often kept in stations, workplaces, schools and community buildings, usually in marked cabinets. Ask someone nearby to fetch one while another person calls emergency services. Check local directories or signs in your area before an emergency.'), (('should i use a defibrillator on a conscious person', 'when not to use a defibrillator with a defibrillator', 'is it safe to use a defibrillator on a child', 'can i use a defibrillator on a wet person', 'what if the defibrillator says no shock', 'should i attach pads before checking breathing with a defibrillator', 'is a defibrillator safe for bystanders', 'what if i am scared to use a defibrillator', 'can i harm someone with a defibrillator', 'when is a defibrillator not appropriate'), 'A defibrillator is for someone who is unresponsive and not breathing normally. It will not shock a person who does not need it, so follow the prompts. Move the person away from standing water and dry the chest if it is wet, then ask a qualified person for help if unsure.'), (('where do i put defibrillator pads', 'how to attach defibrillator pads to a chest', 'what if defibrillator pads will not stick', 'can i use adult pads for a child defibrillator', 'how many pads does a defibrillator have', 'should i remove clothing for defibrillator pads', 'what if the chest is hairy for defibrillator pads', "how to position pads on a woman's chest with a defibrillator", 'do defibrillator pads need to touch skin', 'what to do if pads are out of date with a defibrillator'), "Place the pads on the bare chest as shown in the pictures on the device, usually one high on the right and one lower on the left. Follow the prompts about children's pads. If pads will not stick, ask emergency services for advice and keep CPR going."), (('what do the defibrillator voice prompts mean', 'should i follow the defibrillator instructions', 'what does analyse mean on a defibrillator', 'why does the defibrillator tell me to stand clear', 'what if the defibrillator keeps saying check electrodes', 'how do i know when the shock has been given with a defibrillator', 'should i stop cpr while the defibrillator talks', 'what happens after a defibrillator shock', 'how quickly can i resume compressions with a defibrillator', 'what if the defibrillator battery is flat'), 'Follow the voice prompts exactly: they tell you when to attach pads, when to stand clear and when to resume compressions. After a shock, start CPR again straight away unless the person shows signs of life. Call emergency services if the device fails.'), (('should i do cpr while waiting for a defibrillator', 'how to combine cpr and a defibrillator', 'what to do until the defibrillator arrives', 'should i send someone for a defibrillator', 'how long should compressions continue before a shock with a defibrillator', 'what if the defibrillator arrives late', 'can one person do cpr and fetch the device with a defibrillator', 'how to prioritise cpr and defibrillation with a defibrillator', 'what to do after using a defibrillator during defibrillator use', 'who takes over after a defibrillator is used'), 'Keep doing CPR while someone fetches the defibrillator, and open it as soon as it arrives. Continue compressions during setup, pausing only when the device analyses. Hand over to the ambulance crew and tell them what shocks were delivered.'), (('do i need training to use a defibrillator', 'can an untrained person use a defibrillator', 'should i learn how to use a defibrillator', 'where can i take a defibrillator course', 'is it difficult to operate a defibrillator', 'what skills help with defibrillator use', 'can children use a defibrillator', 'how to practise with a training defibrillator', 'should workplaces teach defibrillator use', 'when to ask for help using a defibrillator'), 'Most public defibrillators are designed for bystanders and give clear spoken instructions, so training is helpful but not essential in an emergency. A first-aid course gives you confidence and practice. Call emergency services and let them guide you if you are unsure.'), (('how do i maintain a defibrillator at work', 'what checks does a defibrillator need', 'how often should defibrillator pads be replaced', 'who is responsible for a defibrillator', 'what if a defibrillator has a fault message', 'how to store a defibrillator safely', 'should a defibrillator be registered', 'what does a defibrillator service involve', 'how to check defibrillator battery life', 'when to call the supplier about a defibrillator'), "Keep the defibrillator in its marked cabinet, check the status light and follow the manufacturer's maintenance schedule. Replace pads and batteries when the device or service record says to. Ask the supplier or a qualified technician if a fault appears."), (('what if the person wakes up after a defibrillator', 'should i move someone after a defibrillator shock', 'how to care for a person after defibrillation with a defibrillator', 'what happens in hospital after a defibrillator', 'should i keep the pads attached with a defibrillator', 'what if the person is confused after a shock with a defibrillator', 'when to start cpr again after defibrillation with a defibrillator', 'what to tell paramedics about the defibrillator', 'how to stay calm after using a defibrillator', 'who can take over after defibrillator use with a defibrillator'), 'If the person wakes or breathes normally after a shock, leave the pads in place and wait with them until help arrives. If they remain unresponsive, resume CPR. Tell the ambulance crew how many shocks were given and when.'), (('when should i call emergency services before using a defibrillator', 'do i call an ambulance for a defibrillator shock', 'what information to give about a defibrillator', 'can i use a defibrillator without calling for help', 'how urgent is it to fetch a defibrillator', 'what if no one else can call while i use it', 'should i call first or fetch the defibrillator first', 'what to say to the operator about defibrillator use', 'when to ask for advice about a defibrillator', 'how to hand over after using a defibrillator'), 'Call emergency services as soon as someone is unresponsive and not breathing normally, and ask others to fetch the defibrillator. Tell the operator where you are and that a device is being used. Follow their instructions until a qualified crew arrives.'))
